<Layout title="Privacy" description="How Two Spoons handles newsletter signups, contact messages, and order requests."><div class="container"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CLARITY</span><h1>Your details,<br/><em>handled with care.</em></h1><p>Our privacy notice · September 27, 2026</p></header><article class="prose"><h2>What you share with us</h2><p>When you sign up for the newsletter, we collect your name, email address, any product interests you choose, your consent, and the signup date. When you send a message, we also save your topic and message.</p><p>Order requests include your selected product lines and quantities, pickup or delivery preference, and any optional phone number and notes. If you request delivery, we collect the address you provide. We do not collect payment card details.</p><h2>How we use it</h2><p>We use these details to manage our newsletter list, answer your questions, and follow up on order requests. Placing an order request or sending a message does not sign you up for marketing unless you separately choose to join the newsletter.</p><h2>How details are stored</h2><p>Submissions are stored in a private database accessible to the people operating Two Spoons and the server hosting the website. We may export them privately to manage requests and the newsletter. The website currently saves submissions without automatically sending a confirmation email.</p><p>We keep details while they’re needed to manage your request or subscription. You can ask us to update or remove them. We do not sell your personal information.</p><h2>Cookies and website activity</h2><p>This website does not use advertising trackers, analytics cookies, or customer accounts. To limit spam, the server temporarily counts submissions by network address in memory. The hosting provider may keep standard technical access logs for operation and security.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>To leave the newsletter, correct your details, or request deletion, use our <a href="/contact?topic=Newsletter%20or%20privacy%20request">contact form</a> and choose “Newsletter or privacy request.” Include the email address you used so we can locate your information. We may need to verify the request before making changes.</p><h2>Keep sensitive details out</h2><p>Please do not include payment card numbers, sensitive medical information, or other private details in forms. If you have a product question, tell us what information would help you choose.</p><h2>If things change</h2><p>We’ll update this notice when our data practices change, including when we connect a newsletter delivery service or add payment processing.</p></article></div></Layout>
